WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:06.500
From a secret hot Invisible Man to monstrous
adult jokes, Hotel Transylvania 4 is packed

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.470
with hilarious¬ references and easter eggs
you might have missed.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:14.059
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan, and
in this video I'm revealing 27 deliciously

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:17.640
dark details and hidden gags the filmmakers
snuck into the movie.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.779
Some spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:26.800
The movie begins with the hotel's 125th Anniversary
party and a spectacular array of monster performances

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.929
organised by Johnny, including the Werewolf
Kids running out on stage with a set of cards

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:33.500
that spell out "Happy Anniversary".

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.989
But in their mad rush, the pups trip and tumble
over each other and as they get up their cards

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:41.379
now read:
Very phine a…

00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:42.850
Ooh, oh no!

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:47.140
The scene quickly moves on, but although it
looks like the name Phineas, there's a crucial

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:53.399
gap so that P, H, I, N and E is pronounced
"fine" and that last S card was going to complete

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:54.789
the end of another word.

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:59.340
You can see the joke in full for just the
tiniest fraction of a second later when Drac

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:04.449
freezes the chaos at the party before he quickly
rearranges the letters to read "Happy Anniversary".

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:09.490
There are some devilishly dark and gruesome
little details you might have easily overlooked

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.030
at the party dinner tables.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:15.630
There's the centrepiece which is not only
made up of flowers, but also tentacles and

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.630
eyeballs.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:21.450
Instead of ordinary forks and knives, the
guests have mini axes and prongs to eat with,

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.310
and then there's the salt and pepper pots
whose design appears to be inspired by the

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:30.150
infamous iron maiden torture devices given
the little spikes on top and the anguished

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.640
faces.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:36.040
When Van Helsing takes Johnny down into his
lab to show him the Monster-fication Ray,

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.509
you can spot a ton of weird and wonderful
objects from the former villain's monster-hunting

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:44.000
days,
including a huge dinosaur skeleton, a mysterious

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.049
humanoid skeleton with horns, a giant robot
outfit, and an old diving suit he might have

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:54.549
used to discover the ancient underwater civilization
of Atlantis.

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:58.810
And hanging from the ceiling is a replica
of the aeroplane he used when hunting Drac

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.750
in Hotel Transylvania 3.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:06.100
Also, there appears to be the body of a giant
shark, which could be what happened to Sharkie,

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.800
one of the monster pets Drac introduced to
Tinkles in the short film Monster Pets!

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:11.800
Sharkie!

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.470
When Van Helsing uses the Monster-fication
Ray on Gigi the gerbil and then on Johnny,

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:21.860
right next to him is a giant circular stone
with an engraving of a tentacled monster,

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:26.730
a secret reference to the Kraken that Van
Helsing hypnotised and used to attack Drac

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:30.000
and the other monsters in Hotel Transylvania
3.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.750
And just like he converted the friendly Kraken
into an angry beast with the Instrument of

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:41.010
Destruction in that movie, in Hotel Transylvania
4 Van Helsing's contraption also slowly turns

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.520
Johnny into a raging uncontrollable monster.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:49.000
And the central part of the stone with the
face and surrounding wave pattern is the secret

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.990
entrance to the ruins of Atlantis from the
third film.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:56.990
It's probably no coincidence either that there's
a portrait of one of Van Helsing's ancestors

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:02.220
from the third movie just outside the elevator
door at the hotel looking on as Drac accidentally

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:06.390
turns himself into a human with the Monster-fication
Ray.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:11.370
Drac tries to hide his transformation from
Mavis, and the other monsters help by distracting

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.350
her with Wayne's new dance moves.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:18.150
The routine he tries to do is inspired by
real-life social media dance challenges, in

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:24.150
particular the viral hit "Renegade" dance
created by Jalailah Harmon.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:27.170
Oh, yeah.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:32.450
And speaking of social media stars, the character
of Party Monster is played by streamer "Ninja",

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.110
aka Tyler Blevins.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.440
Oh yeah.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.540
When Griffin becomes human, the Drac Pack
is shocked to learn that he's been naked from

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:44.190
the moment we first met him, a little hat-tip
to the fans of the franchise who guessed this

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:47.570
early on:
Have you seriously been naked this whole time?

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.570
Uh, yeah.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:51.010
Why would only my glasses be visible?

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:55.250
Notice how he has red curly hair as he explained
in the first movie.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.390
What's wrong with red, curly hair?

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:58.600
Why are you getting upset?

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.420
I have red curly hair!

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:06.520
Now, Griffin's human form as a balding, pot-bellied,
middle-aged man caused a bit of a stir among

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.620
some Hotel Transylvania fans when the movie's
trailer came out.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:16.579
Over 30,000 people signed a petition on behalf
of "The Invisible Man Simps Community" asking

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:19.440
Sony Animation to make Griffin hot.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:24.010
And it's possible the filmmakers give a little
nod to this because they actually snuck an

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:27.480
alternate version of Griffin into the final
movie.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:33.000
To catch this, watch really carefully during
the crystal cave scene because as broken reflections

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:38.020
of each character appear in the giant crystals,
when Griffin wanders into view, in the corner

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:43.810
there's a design of him that's completely
different including a full head of hair.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:44.810
I'm inviz.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:48.470
Man, just because you're invisible doesn't
mean you get to be naked.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.930
Gremlin Air makes a hilarious return for the
fourth movie and there's a bit of humorous

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:57.820
lampshading that acknowledges how ridiculous
it is that the plane can actually fly.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.820
How is this plane even in the sky?!

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.190
Is that duct tape holding the wing together?!

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:08.240
After arriving in South America, Johnny and
Drac take a bus to the Amazon but when Johnny's

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:13.370
monster size slows it down, he decides to
move the vehicle along by picking it up and

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.430
running with it,
a shout-out to the old school animation The

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:21.130
Flintstones where Fred and his friend Barney
would sometimes use foot power to literally

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.370
run their car.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.530
There's a long-running joke in the franchise
that Drac supposedly goes around saying " bleh,

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:28.530
bleh-bleh".

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:29.550
Yes, fellow Dracula.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:30.780
There's only one way.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:31.780
Bleh, bleh-bleh.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.800
Bleh, bleh-bleh.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.430
I don't know where that comes from.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:41.420
And it's true that according to Vampires.com,
Dracula has never said the phrase either in

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:45.860
the books or the live-action movies that came
before the animated movie franchise.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:50.890
However, in Hotel Transylvania 4, as Drac
tries to explain why he made up the monster

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:53.080
real estate law, he says...

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.300
Johnny found out that I was giving you guys
the hotel.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.900
But then he
had a Johnny takeover:

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.750
escalators, name changes, blah, blah, blah.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:06.210
Although Ericka gave up her monster-hunting
ways at the end of the third movie, when she

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:10.950
goes in search of Drac and Johnny, she gets
some of her old monster-hunting contraptions

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:11.950
out again.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:16.310
There's her blimp which is full of lethal
weapons,

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:17.310
Okay.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:21.360
Yeah, it's a death trap.
and the tank-like armoured vehicle she drives

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.260
has a license plate that reads "MNSTR HNTR".

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:29.360
The jeep also has a V-shaped ornament as a
nod to her family name, just like the car

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:31.990
her great granddaddy chased Drac with.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:36.480
When the gang eventually arrive at the Crystal
Cave, they enter through an opening that looks

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.010
like the jaws of a monster.

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:43.550
And when the cave begins to collapse later
on, as Frank and Eunice run from the falling

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:47.350
rocks they both say
If he ruins my hair, I'm never gonna forgive

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:48.350
him!

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:51.400
That's a funny call-back to the third movie
where Eunice was playing volleyball and was

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.669
worried about getting her hair wet.

00:06:53.669 --> 00:06:56.200
Everybody, just please watch the hair.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.620
Watch the hair!

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:01.471
And the way the gang shield Mavis from the
sun's rays at the end of the movie, as she

00:07:01.471 --> 00:07:06.240
runs to reach Johnny and turn him back into
a human, is a neat parallel to how Drac was

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:10.530
shielded from the sun as he raced to reach
Johnny at the end of the first movie.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.380
Don't worry we got you covered.

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:16.780
The way the wolf pups extend in a line to
provide shade for Mavis is similar to how

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:21.230
the townspeople formed a line to cover Drac
in the original film.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:25.120
And something you might not have noticed is
that the voice of Drac changed for this fourth

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.480
film from Adam Sandler who played him in the
first three movies to voice actor, impressionist,

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.551
and YouTuber Brian Hull.

00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:36.750
Hull already voiced Drac in the short film
Monster Pets and does an excellent job in

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.320
the new feature sounding uncannily like Sandler's
Drac.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.570
Thank you Johnny.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:42.910
How wonderful.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:48.470
So, what did you think of the fourth and final
Hotel Transylvania movie and how it ended?

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:50.230
And who are your favourite characters?

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:52.540
Leave your thoughts in the comments below.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:56.720
If you enjoyed this video then do hit that
like button, I really appreciate it.

